<title>SWITZERLAND: SAirGroup says no plans to quit Sabena.</title>
<headline>SAirGroup says no plans to quit Sabena.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hannes Goetz, chairman of SAirGroup, said Sabena's 1996 loss was disappointing, but not surprising and there were no plans at all to withdraw from the Belgian carrier.</p>
<p>Asked whether a withdrawal from Sabena was an issue, Goetz told the Swiss daily Tages-Anzeiger:</p>
<p>&quot;No. We will continue and intensify our cooperation with our Belgian partner in various areas.&quot;</p>
<p>SAirGroup is the holding company for the Swissair airline.</p>
<p>On Wednesday Sabena, in which SAirGroup owns 49.5 percent, reported an 8.9 billion Belgian franc loss.</p>
</text>
